  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Jeffrey Springs shut down Seattle over seven scoreless innings, and the offense took care of the rest.",
    "what_this_means": "This is what happens when the starter you need actually shows up. Springs gave the Athletics everything. Complete control, no walks, six strikeouts through seven. And they made it count. Max Muncy drove in two early, then Lawrence Butler broke it open with a two-run eighth that put the game away at 6-0. The lineup didn't need to be dynamic. It needed to not waste good pitching, and for once, it didn't. Geoff Hartlieb and Elvis Alvarado each threw a scoreless inning to close it out. Four straight wins now. The streak is real because the starter gave them room to breathe.",
